      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): honor repeated response content lengths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where OpenClaw script helpers could ignore repeated equivalent `Content-Length` declarations and only discover an oversized response after starting to read the body.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe script bounded-response helper now canonicalizes valid decimal length tokens before comparing comma-combined declarations, while preserving streaming enforcement for conflicting or malformed values. The TypeScript and JavaScript script helpers stay aligned.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAutomation and local tooling fail earlier for oversized responses even when an intermediary repeats the same decimal `Content-Length` value with different padding, without changing behavior for conflicting or malformed declarations.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current head: `4800a935c5ee66cd85e5b9207c434b0b068603a2`.\n- Runtime proof: `node --input-type=module -` exercised both production helpers, `scripts/lib/bounded-response.ts` and `scripts/lib/bounded-response.mjs`.\n\n```text\nhead=4800a935c5ee66cd85e5b9207c434b0b068603a2\nts 17, 017 => error=probe response body exceeded 16 bytes. readStarted=false canceled=true\nts 17, 12 => error=probe response body exceeded 16 bytes. readStarted=true canceled=true\nmjs 17, 017 => error=probe response body exceeded 16 bytes readStarted=false canceled=true\nmjs 17, 12 => error=probe response body exceeded 16 bytes readStarted=true canceled=true\n```\n\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check` passed.\n- Current-head checks: `Real behavior proof` passed; `checks-node-changed` and `checks-node-changed-boundary` passed.",
